    "text": "<p>A parallel-plate capacitor with plate area <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> has separation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi></math> between the plates. Two dielectric slabs of dielectric constant <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> of same area <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;and thickness <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;are inserted in the space between the plates. The capacitance of the capacitor will be given by :</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/d8620034-b4b3-48fd-a6b0-abac0305b771-image.png\" style=\"width: 253px; height: 227px;\" /></p>",
